{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncur=[i for i in json.load(open('state.json'))['interpretations'] if i['id'].startswith('8045c255')][0]\nkn={k['id']:k for k in json.load(open('state.json'))['knowledge']}\nex=\\\"a319426e86514f45b2053a7b3bd8050b\\\"\nprint(cur['rationale'][:900])\nprint('---')\nprint(len(cur['rationale']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Conclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. A leadership transfer that explicitly names a member the configuration marks as a non-voter is admitted, completes its future without error, and does not install that member as leader; the attempt instead forces an election round in which every member's term advances, leadership lands on a member the caller did not name, and leadership is absent for a measurable interval. Evidence, five receipts of the same experiment lineage. Parsed index 1 of receipt d436029b08c5425aa5aec577901cb8ba and of successor receipt 0726bba116ac415fa38b99b96a88290f, the control where the explicit target is an ordinary voter: target_ever_leader=true, final_leader_is_target=true, future_ok=true, target_term_after=3 with other_member_term_max_after=3, so the mechanism installs the named target with a single term advance. Parsed index 3 of both receipts, the \n---\n5165\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncur=[i for i in json.load(open('state.json'))['interpretations'] if i['id'].startswith('8045c255')][0]\nkn={k['id']:k for k in json.load(open('state.json'))['knowledge']}\nex=\\\"a319426e86514f45b2053a7b3bd8050b\\\"\n\nrat=cur['rationale'].replace(\n \\\"is admitted, completes its future without error, and does not install that member as leader;\\\",\n \\\"is admitted without any refusal keyed to its suffrage and does not install that member as leader;\\\")\n\npara=(\\\"Entry-point comparison, receipt %s (completed, tests_passed, exit 0): one four-member cluster per case, one follower demoted in each, and the demoted member's own configuration view reporting the non-voter role before the transfer, converging in 0 ms in the control and 6 ms in the trigger. Parsed index 0 records the control's state and parsed index 1 its result: the automatic LeadershipTransfer() needed one attempt, its future returned nil in 106 ms, leadership ended on a voter that is not the demoted member, no leaderless sample was seen in 26 samples over three seconds, and a client Apply and a GetConfiguration afterwards both succeeded. Parsed index 2 records the trigger's state and parsed index 3 its result: five attempts spanning 1035 ms each returned 'leadership transfer in progress', the named member never reported Leader across the same 26 samples, the final leader is a different voter, and the client Apply and GetConfiguration afterwards both succeeded. The control therefore shows that transfer works on this cluster shape and that the automatic path avoids the demoted member, while the explicit path admits the named member, keeps reporting a transfer in progress, and never installs it; both the earlier nil futures and this receipt's in-progress errors are consistent with the same gap, since neither is a refusal keyed to the target's lack of a vote.\\\" % ex)\n\nces=list(cur['counterevidence'])\nces.append(\\\"The future's result is not uniform across receipts: the demotion race receipt 62e8b8bdcc9f448687b6588dda84125d recorded successful transfer futures in all twenty attempts, while receipt %s recorded 'leadership transfer in progress' on every one of five attempts on a four-member cluster whose demoted member's view had already converged. The sentence that the future completes without error therefore describes those receipts and not the operation in general, and the durable observation common to both is that the named member is never installed and no suffrage check refuses it.\\\" % ex)\n\nlims=list(cur['limitations'])\nlims.append(\\\"Receipt %s does not establish whether the in-progress error comes from a transfer that was already running when the call arrived or from the call itself: the harness does not sample the leader's transfer flag immediately before the first attempt, and its five attempts are only about a second apart. It also measures a single demotion and a single transfer per case.\\\" % ex)\n\njoint=cur['joint_history']+(\\\" Receipt %s comes from a further experiment identifier, 6f0e1da8cb8048f5b28060a73243fa6b-experiment, which keeps the same demote-then-transfer shape and adds an automatic-transfer control on the same four-member cluster shape plus a client write after the transfer attempt.\\\" % ex)\n\nk0=kn['f7da39e9771e40d29f8d7ec3d1c7d886-knowledge-0']\nk1=kn['f7da39e9771e40d29f8d7ec3d1c7d886-knowledge-1']\ne0=dict(k0['executions']); e0[ex]=[0,2]\ne1=dict(k1['executions']); e1[ex]=[1,3]\n\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpret receipt %s, the paired experiment that adds an automatic-transfer control on the same cluster shape as the explicit transfer to a demoted member. The control completed and handed leadership to a voter while the explicit attempt never installed the named member and reported a transfer in progress on every attempt, so the account keeps its violated conclusion and asserted defect claim, replaces the claim that the future completes without error with the weaker and better supported claim that the target is never refused for lacking a vote, and records the discrepancy plus the open question about where the in-progress state comes from.\\\" % ex,\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":k0['id'],\\\"kind\\\":k0['kind'],\\\"statement\\\":k0['statement'],\\\"conditions\\\":k0['conditions'],\\\"source_ids\\\":k0['source_ids'],\\\"executions\\\":e0},\n  {\\\"id\\\":k1['id'],\\\"kind\\\":k1['kind'],\\\"statement\\\":k1['statement'],\\\"conditions\\\":k1['conditions'],\\\"source_ids\\\":k1['source_ids'],\\\"executions\\\":e1},\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"f7da39e9771e40d29f8d7ec3d1c7d886-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"6f0e1da8cb8048f5b28060a73243fa6b-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{ex:[0,1,2,3]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":rat+\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\"+para,\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":ces,\n  \\\"limitations\\\":lims,\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":joint,\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":k0['id'],\\\"revision\\\":k0['revision']+1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"An explicit transfer target is resolved only through leaderState.replState, which includes non-voters, while pickServer skips non-voters.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":k1['id'],\\\"revision\\\":k1['revision']+1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"A voter adopts a higher term and steps down before rejecting a configured non-voter candidate, and timeoutNow forces candidacy without checking suffrage or term.\\\"},\n  ],\n }],\n}\njson.dump(upd, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nprint('written')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
